// P7 refusal fixture — a binary built WITHOUT the debug-info sidecar, so `maxon profile` has nothing to
// symbolize with and must say so by name.
//
// ⭐ IT NEEDS ITS OWN SOURCE FILE, and that is not tidiness. `--no-debug-info` does not change a single
// byte of the executable (the sidecar is a separate file), so the build cache treats a `--no-debug-info`
// build of an already-built source as CURRENT and hands back the cached binary — leaving the earlier
// `.mxdbg` sitting next to it, still matching, still usable. Pointing this block at a source some other
// golden builds normally would therefore have profiled it SUCCESSFULLY and asserted a refusal that never
// happened. Nothing else builds this file, so it has never had a sidecar to leave behind.
//
// The program itself is deliberately trivial: the refusal happens before it is ever launched.

typealias ExitCode = int(0 to 255)

function main() returns ExitCode
	print("unreachable by profile: this binary has no sidecar\n")

	return 0
end 'main'
